import Matchsticks.Basic

/-! The certificate assigns each of the 32768 frontier states two five-bit
potential values. Value 31 means unreachable. For each of the five digits,
a bit set stores which states have digit zero. The hexadecimal words below
run from high state indices to low indices, in groups of 512 states.

These data were found by recording the smallest value of `3 * cost - 10 * width`
for each legal width-one state, then minimizing over legal column extensions
with weight `3 * addedCost - 10` until the values stabilized. The second table
is the corresponding minimum just after the horizontal edges are processed.
The proof only uses the verified initial and transition inequalities.

The checkers use sets of states whose potential is at most a threshold.
Reading digits from low to high, a zero threshold digit intersects the
current set with the zero-digit set, and a one threshold digit takes the
union. The transition proofs verify all claimed bounds from these data.
-/
namespace Matchsticks.BitSets

private def pack (words : Array Nat) : Nat :=
  words.foldl (fun acc word => (acc <<< 512) ||| word) 0

private def threshold (planes : Array Nat) (k : Nat) : Nat :=
  (List.range 5).foldl (fun acc i =>
    if k.testBit i then planes[i]! ||| acc else planes[i]! &&& acc
  ) ((1 <<< 32768) - 1)

